# Cells

Every kind of HQL fence. The body of each is coloured as HQL, and the line
that opens it has four parts with a colour each: the language, the `#`, the
mode, and the attributes.

## A cell that shows its value

```hql#eval id=languages
/// The `metadata` block in the header of a catalog card.
type Meta { year : Int, typing : String, grammar : String }
type Header : Data { metadata? : Meta }

type Language { name : String, year : Int, typing : String, grammar : String }

cards
| filter(c => c.path.starts_with("catalog/") and c.name != "index")
| flat_map(c => match (c.header | Header).metadata {
    some(m) => [Language(name = c.title, year = m.year, typing = m.typing, grammar = m.grammar)],
    _ => []
})
| sort(by = l => l.year)
```
<!-- hql:output id=languages hash=2cd4baa0a239 status=ok -->
- Language(name = "Python", year = 1991, typing = "dynamic", grammar = "built-in")
- Language(name = "Kotlin", year = 2011, typing = "static", grammar = "install")
- Language(name = "TypeScript", year = 2012, typing = "static", grammar = "built-in")
- Language(name = "Rust", year = 2015, typing = "static", grammar = "built-in")
- Language(name = "Zig", year = 2016, typing = "static", grammar = "install")
- Language(name = "HQL", year = 2026, typing = "static", grammar = "extension")
<!-- /hql:output -->

## A cell other cells read

`hql#query` is `hql#eval hidden`: it computes a value and shows nothing.

```hql#query id=installable
languages | filter(l => l.grammar == "install")
```

```hql#eval id=static hidden
languages | filter(l => l.typing == "static" and not (l.grammar == "install"))
```

## A table

```hql#eval
// Where the grammar of each language comes from.
fn source(grammar: String) : String = match grammar {
    "built-in" => "the editor",
    "extension" => "this extension",
    _ => "an extension to install"
}

languages
| map(l => { "Language": l.name, "Since": l.year, "Grammar from": source(l.grammar) })
| Table(columns = ["Language", "Since", "Grammar from"])
| format(as = Markdown)
```
<!-- hql:output hash=09a58d02dd9c status=ok -->
| Language   | Since | Grammar from            |
| ---------- | ----- | ----------------------- |
| Python     | 1991  | the editor              |
| Kotlin     | 2011  | an extension to install |
| TypeScript | 2012  | the editor              |
| Rust       | 2015  | the editor              |
| Zig        | 2016  | an extension to install |
| HQL        | 2026  | this extension          |
<!-- /hql:output -->

## A record

```hql#eval
{
    languages: languages | size,
    to_install: installable | size,
    static_and_ready: static | size,
    oldest: languages | map(l => l.year) | min | unwrap_or(0)
}
```
<!-- hql:output hash=a99ab0cad2b7 status=ok -->
| key              | value |
| ---------------- | ----- |
| languages        | 6     |
| oldest           | 1991  |
| static_and_ready | 3     |
| to_install       | 2     |
<!-- /hql:output -->

## Literals and operators

```hql#eval
// A string with escapes, an Int, a Decimal, a Float, and a comparison chain.
{
    text: "tab\there, quote \"here\", slash \\ here",
    whole: 10 % 3 - -4,
    exact: 1.5 * 2.25,
    rough: 1.5f * 2.0e3f,
    truth: true and not false or 1 <= 2,
    choice: "few" given (languages | size) < 3 otherwise "many"
}
```
<!-- hql:output hash=7f736bc41d11 status=ok -->
| key    | value                                      |
| ------ | ------------------------------------------ |
| choice | "many"                                     |
| exact  | 3.375                                      |
| rough  | 3000.0                                     |
| text   | "tab\there, quote \"here\", slash \\ here" |
| truth  | true                                       |
| whole  | 5                                          |
<!-- /hql:output -->

## A document reference

```hql#eval
@[[catalog]].title
```
<!-- hql:output hash=48e5ae338462 status=ok -->
Catalog
<!-- /hql:output -->

## A listing is not a cell

A fence marked plain `hql` is shown as code and never runs. It is coloured the
same way.

```hql
cards | filter(c => c.title == "HQL") | map(c => c.path) | first
```

## Tildes

~~~hql#eval id=names
languages | map(l => l.name)
~~~
